      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can tell you're worried, but I'm here to reassure you. Your husband's symptoms are a bit more concerning than just being \"wiped out\" from being sick. The fever, headache, and lethargy could be signs of a more serious complication, like pneumonia or sinusitis. I'm not saying he needs to go to the ER, but I would recommend a more cautious approach. Give him the Tylenol and naproxen, but also make sure he drinks plenty of fluids, like water and clear broths, to stay hydrated. And yes, a double dose of Tylenol is fine, but don't overdo it - 1200mg of acetaminophen is a safe maximum.",
